 Restart;t
⍝ Restart the broadcast loop with the current #.Ex3.Broadcast, keeping the server running (supplied: you don't need to change this)
⍝ Use it after editing Broadcast with )ED: the loop that is already running keeps its old code until it is restarted.
⍝ Don't use Run3 for this: Run3 reloads the code from the files, which would throw away your edits.
⍝ Run3 loads this function.
⍝ Usage: Restart
 :If 9≠⌊#.⎕NC'Ex3Server'
 :OrIf ~#.Ex3Server.Running
     ⎕←'Problem: the server is not running; start it with Run3'
     →0
 :EndIf
⍝ End the current loop: Broadcast checks Running every time round. Wait up to 3 seconds, then stop it anyway
 #.Ex3.Running←0
 :If 2=#.⎕NC'Ex3Thread'
     t←⎕AI[3]+3000
     :While (#.Ex3Thread∊⎕TNUMS)∧⎕AI[3]<t
         ⎕DL 0.1
     :EndWhile
     ⎕TKILL #.Ex3Thread∩⎕TNUMS
 :EndIf
⍝ Start the loop again, with the Broadcast that is defined now
 #.Ex3.Running←1
 #.Ex3Thread←#.Ex3.Broadcast&#.Ex3Server
 ⎕←'Broadcast loop restarted with the current code'
